selfirmiss: a self-compile function in a shape the IR misses (`for x in xs` over an `f32[]`),
reached from bignumReset with no change in behaviour. It is aimed at the `self ir misses` row.
Reading 2026-11-23 on ir-self-miss-ratchet (#9701), gate.sh --fast: `self ir misses` FAILED
(`1 for in element f32`), every other row ok. No other row reads the self-compile's IR census,
and identity cannot see a miss, because a missed function falls back to legacy under both seeds.

